  "note": "ALG/LB: the first 120 min of week 101 (5-min routing, reduced menu) over the LP bound, an upper bound on the ratio to the offline optimum. $p^\\ast$: lower median over week 101 of the first i.i.d.\\ reclaim probability with $r_0>1$ (0.00: $r_0>1$ already without reclaims; none: $r_0\\le1$ at every $p\\le1$; $>$0.2: likewise, but only $p\\le0.2$ ran). Guarded rows: per-group allowance $\\min\\{\\Wk,\\mathrm{LB}'\\}$. Theorem~\\ref{thm:fullmodel}'s bound held in 28 of 28 guarded runs (trace, five stress and honoring lenders; 7 of Lagged RetroRenting + one-way guard (\\mbox{$B_0=10\\%$} of the all-fallback bill); cases (a) 14, (b) 14); Corollary~\\ref{cor:ratio}(b) holds for Sublet and Sublet, one-way, on core instances (Lemma~\\ref{lem:projection}(e)); Sublet, one-way aborted in 7 of 7 runs (under the trace lender in 1 of 1 week, at 1.003 times the all-fallback bill); Sublet and Greedy + guard in none. Primary baselines (H1): Greedy renting; Greedy, back-off; RetroRenting-style; Per-borrower ski rental; SpotHedge-style, \\mbox{$N_{\\mathrm{Extra}}=0$}; CoCaR-style; and RetroRenting-style, lagged (supplement). Provision for peak: 5.9 times the all-fallback bill in overflow accounting.",
